# Let-gen polymorphism: f is polymorphically generalized (Kiselyov 2013 levels-based let-gen).
# It can be called at both Int and String in the same dict scope without a type error.
[f: [fn [x@a] x]
 r1: [f 42]
 r2: [f "hello"]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x), "r1": Int(42), "r2": String("hello")})

